# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setup {#setup}"
msgstr "Persediaan {#setup}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Import the libraries used throughout the tutorial and fix a random seed for reproducibility.\n"
msgstr "Import pustaka yang digunakan sepanjang tutorial dan tetapkan benih rawak untuk kebolehulangan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Small-scale simulator example {#small-scale-simulator-example}"
msgstr "Contoh simulator skala kecil {#small-scale-simulator-example}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We start with eight assets drawn from six sectors and select exactly $K=4$ of them. With only eight assets there are only $\\binom{8}{4}=70$ valid portfolios, so we can later check the quantum result against an exhaustive search.\n"
msgstr "Kita bermula dengan lapan aset yang diambil daripada enam sektor dan memilih tepat $K=4$ daripadanya. Dengan hanya lapan aset, hanya ada $\\binom{8}{4}=70$ portfolio sah, jadi kita boleh menyemak hasil kuantum kemudian dengan carian menyeluruh.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Langkah 1: Petakan input klasik kepada masalah kuantum {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each asset is one qubit; a bitstring like `10110010` is a portfolio (the 1s are the assets we hold). We need three ingredients: the market data, the three objective Hamiltonians, and a circuit that only ever proposes portfolios with exactly $K$ assets.\n"
msgstr "Setiap aset ialah satu qubit; bitstring seperti `10110010` ialah satu portfolio (angka 1 ialah aset yang kita pegang). Kita perlukan tiga bahan: data pasaran, tiga Hamiltonian objektif, dan litar yang hanya mencadangkan portfolio dengan tepat $K$ aset.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Enforcing \"exactly K assets\" without a penalty.** A common trick is to add a penalty term that punishes portfolios of the wrong size, but that couples every qubit to every other qubit, which leads to much deeper circuits after transpilation. Instead we use an **XY mixer**, which only ever moves the QAOA state *between* bitstrings of the same Hamming weight. If we start in a state that already has $K$ assets selected, every portfolio the circuit explores also has exactly $K$ assets. The constraint is built into the circuit's structure rather than enforced by a penalty term.\n"
msgstr "**Menguatkuasakan \"tepat K aset\" tanpa penalti.** Helah biasa ialah menambah sebutan penalti yang menghukum portfolio bersaiz salah, tetapi itu menggandingkan setiap qubit dengan setiap qubit lain, yang membawa kepada litar yang jauh lebih dalam selepas transpilasi. Sebaliknya kita menggunakan **pencampur XY**, yang hanya menggerakkan keadaan QAOA *antara* bitstring yang berberat Hamming sama. Jika kita bermula dalam keadaan yang sudah mempunyai $K$ aset terpilih, setiap portfolio yang diterokai litar juga mempunyai tepat $K$ aset. Kekangan itu dibina ke dalam struktur litar dan bukannya dikuatkuasakan oleh sebutan penalti.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We prepare the starting state cheaply: rotate each qubit so it is \"on\" with probability $K/N$. Restricted to the $K$-asset outcomes, this reproduces the ideal equal-weight (Dicke) state, so we simply keep the measured bitstrings that have exactly $K$ ones — a step called *post-selection*.\n"
msgstr "Kita menyediakan keadaan permulaan dengan murah: putarkan setiap qubit supaya ia \"hidup\" dengan kebarangkalian $K/N$. Dihadkan kepada hasil $K$ aset, ini menghasilkan semula keadaan berberat sama (Dicke) yang unggul, jadi kita hanya mengekalkan bitstring terukur yang mempunyai tepat $K$ angka satu — langkah yang dipanggil *pascapemilihan*.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Langkah 2: Optimumkan masalah untuk pelaksanaan perkakasan kuantum {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before running, the abstract circuit is transpiled into hardware-native gates. At this small scale we only inspect the cost: how deep is the circuit and how many two-qubit gates does it use? (Two-qubit gates are the main source of noise on real devices.)\n"
msgstr "Sebelum dijalankan, litar abstrak ditranspile menjadi gate natif perkakasan. Pada skala kecil ini kita hanya memeriksa kosnya: seberapa dalam litar itu dan berapa banyak gate dua-qubit yang digunakannya? (Gate dua-qubit ialah punca utama hingar pada peranti sebenar.)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"
msgstr "Langkah 3: Laksanakan menggunakan primitif Qiskit {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two stages. First we **train** the QAOA angles once, using equal objective weights, with an exact statevector simulator to find good $\\beta,\\gamma$ values. Then we **sweep** many weight vectors across the simplex and sample the circuit at each, collecting candidate portfolios. Because only the objective weights change between sweeps (not the trained angles), all the weight vectors are submitted in a single batched job.\n"
msgstr "Dua peringkat. Mula-mula kita **melatih** sudut QAOA sekali, menggunakan pemberat objektif yang sama, dengan simulator vektor keadaan tepat untuk mencari nilai $\\beta,\\gamma$ yang baik. Kemudian kita **menyapu** banyak vektor pemberat merentasi simpleks dan mensampel litar pada setiap satu, mengumpul portfolio calon. Oleh sebab hanya pemberat objektif yang berubah antara sapuan (bukan sudut terlatih), semua vektor pemberat dihantar dalam satu job kelompok.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr "Langkah 4: Pasca-proses dan pulangkan hasil dalam format klasik yang dikehendaki {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We keep only the feasible portfolios (exactly $K$ assets from the post-selection step), score each one on all three objectives, and extract the **Pareto front**: the portfolios that are not beaten on every objective at once. The *hypervolume* is a single number summarizing how much objective space the front dominates, and bigger is better.\n"
msgstr "Kita hanya mengekalkan portfolio yang boleh laksana (tepat $K$ aset daripada langkah pascapemilihan), menilai setiap satu pada ketiga-tiga objektif, dan mengekstrak **barisan hadapan Pareto**: portfolio yang tidak dikalahkan pada setiap objektif serentak. *Hipervolum* ialah satu nombor yang meringkaskan seberapa banyak ruang objektif yang didominasi barisan itu, dan lebih besar lebih baik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With 100,000 shots over only 256 bitstrings, this run sees every one of the 70 valid portfolios, so at this size it is effectively a brute-force check that the pipeline is wired correctly, rather than evidence that QAOA found the front.\n"
msgstr "Dengan 100,000 tembakan ke atas hanya 256 bitstring, larian ini melihat kesemua 70 portfolio sah, jadi pada saiz ini ia secara berkesan merupakan semakan daya kasar bahawa saluran paip disambung dengan betul, dan bukan bukti bahawa QAOA menemui barisan hadapan.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/quantum-approximate-multi-objective-optimization/extracted-outputs/9ccde65a-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/quantum-approximate-multi-objective-optimization/extracted-outputs/9ccde65a-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Large-scale hardware example {#large-scale-hardware-example}"
msgstr "Contoh perkakasan skala besar {#large-scale-hardware-example}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now the same workflow on **40 assets** (8 sectors × 5), choosing $K=6$. Forty qubits is too large to simulate exactly (a $2^{40}$-amplitude statevector), so the angles can't be optimized the way they were at eight assets, and a dense circuit would be too deep for current hardware. The $\\binom{40}{6} \\approx 3.8$M valid portfolios are still few enough to enumerate classically, which we use at the end as an exact benchmark. Several things change, and **nothing else about the method does**:\n"
msgstr "Sekarang aliran kerja yang sama pada **40 aset** (8 sektor × 5), memilih $K=6$. Empat puluh qubit terlalu besar untuk disimulasi secara tepat (vektor keadaan $2^{40}$ amplitud), jadi sudut tidak boleh dioptimumkan seperti pada lapan aset, dan litar padat akan terlalu dalam untuk perkakasan semasa. $\\binom{40}{6} \\approx 3.8$J portfolio sah masih cukup sedikit untuk dienumerasi secara klasik, yang kita gunakan pada akhirnya sebagai penanda aras tepat. Beberapa perkara berubah, dan **tiada yang lain tentang kaedah ini berubah**:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Train the angles with a matrix-product-state (MPS) simulator, not exact statevector.** Following the reference (Kotil et al.), we fix the objective weights to equal values, optimize a single β, γ on the MPS simulator, and reuse them for every weighting vector in the sweep. (We train at the size we run — no small-to-large angle transfer.)\n"
msgstr "**Latih sudut dengan simulator keadaan hasil darab matriks (MPS), bukan vektor keadaan tepat.** Mengikut rujukan (Kotil et al.), kita tetapkan pemberat objektif kepada nilai sama, optimumkan satu β, γ pada simulator MPS, dan guna semula untuk setiap vektor pemberat dalam sapuan. (Kita melatih pada saiz yang kita jalankan — tiada pemindahan sudut kecil-ke-besar.)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Sparsify the risk model to fit hardware.** A full covariance couples all 780 asset pairs. We keep only the strongest, cheapest-to-route couplings using *importance-aware QAP truncation*, and couple each sector in a light ring for the diversity term. This keeps the objectives meaningful while holding the circuit to a hardware-friendly size.\n"
msgstr "**Jarangkan model risiko supaya muat pada perkakasan.** Kovarians penuh menggandingkan kesemua 780 pasangan aset. Kita hanya mengekalkan gandingan terkuat dan termurah untuk dihalakan menggunakan *pemangkasan QAP sedar kepentingan*, dan menggandingkan setiap sektor dalam gelang ringan untuk sebutan kepelbagaian. Ini memastikan objektif kekal bermakna sambil mengekalkan litar pada saiz mesra perkakasan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Keep the circuit shallow and score honestly.** Routing is stochastic, so we transpile with several seeds and keep the shallowest (and no quantum time is spent). Portfolios are always **scored against the true, full objectives**. The sparsification only shapes the circuit, not how portfolios are judged.\n"
msgstr "**Pastikan litar cetek dan nilai dengan jujur.** Penghalaan bersifat stokastik, jadi kita transpile dengan beberapa benih dan kekalkan yang paling cetek (dan tiada masa kuantum digunakan). Portfolio sentiasa **dinilai terhadap objektif penuh yang sebenar**. Penjarangan hanya membentuk litar, bukan cara portfolio dinilai.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Why QAP truncation?\">\n"
"Keeping each asset's largest couplings by magnitude alone can result in a circuit that is sparse but still awkward to route. QAP truncation instead keeps couplings that are both large *and* physically close on the chip, so the same gate budget buys a shallower, more hardware-friendly circuit.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Mengapa pemangkasan QAP?\">\n"
"Mengekalkan gandingan terbesar setiap aset mengikut magnitud sahaja boleh menghasilkan litar yang jarang tetapi masih sukar dihalakan. Pemangkasan QAP sebaliknya mengekalkan gandingan yang besar *dan* dekat secara fizikal pada cip, jadi bajet gate yang sama membeli litar yang lebih cetek dan lebih mesra perkakasan.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map inputs (sparsified for hardware) {#step-1-map-inputs-sparsified-for-hardware}"
msgstr "Langkah 1: Petakan input (dijarangkan untuk perkakasan) {#step-1-map-inputs-sparsified-for-hardware}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Steps 2-3: train the angles, then build and submit the hardware job {#steps-2-3-train-the-angles-then-build-and-submit-the-hardware-job}"
msgstr "Langkah 2-3: latih sudut, kemudian bina dan hantar job perkakasan {#steps-2-3-train-the-angles-then-build-and-submit-the-hardware-job}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Forty qubits is too large to optimize the angles exactly, so we train one $\\beta, \\gamma$ on a\n"
"matrix-product-state simulator at equal objective weights and reuse them across the sweep.\n"
"The cell below loads pre-trained values from a file. The trained cost-layer angle is small\n"
"($\\gamma \\approx 0.32$), so the circuit applies a gentle bias rather than a sharp projection.\n"
msgstr ""
"Empat puluh qubit terlalu besar untuk mengoptimumkan sudut secara tepat, jadi kita melatih satu $\\beta, \\gamma$ pada\n"
"simulator keadaan hasil darab matriks dengan pemberat objektif sama dan menggunakannya semula merentasi sapuan.\n"
"Sel di bawah memuatkan nilai pralatih daripada fail. Sudut lapisan kos yang terlatih adalah kecil\n"
"($\\gamma \\approx 0.32$), jadi litar mengenakan pincang lembut dan bukannya unjuran tajam.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process into the Pareto front and read off the optimal portfolios {#step-4-post-process-into-the-pareto-front-and-read-off-the-optimal-portfolios}"
msgstr "Langkah 4: Pasca-proses menjadi barisan hadapan Pareto dan baca portfolio optimum {#step-4-post-process-into-the-pareto-front-and-read-off-the-optimal-portfolios}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "At this problem size, QAOA performs about as well as uniform random sampling. Both recover a large fraction of the exact optimum's hypervolume, and neither is clearly ahead. This outcome is expected for a single shallow QAOA layer with a heavily truncated cost operator on noisy hardware; the value of this example is the end-to-end multi-objective workflow (mapping, angle training, constrained sampling, and Pareto post-processing), not a quantum speed-up. Narrowing the gap to the optimum would call for deeper circuits (more QAOA layers), a gentler truncation, or lower-noise hardware.\n"
msgstr "Pada saiz masalah ini, QAOA berprestasi lebih kurang sama baik dengan pensampelan rawak seragam. Kedua-duanya memulihkan sebahagian besar hipervolum optimum tepat, dan tiada yang jelas mendahului. Hasil ini dijangka bagi satu lapisan QAOA cetek dengan operator kos yang dipangkas dengan banyak pada perkakasan berhingar; nilai contoh ini ialah aliran kerja pelbagai objektif hujung ke hujung (pemetaan, latihan sudut, pensampelan terkekang, dan pasca-pemprosesan Pareto), bukan pecutan kuantum. Merapatkan jurang kepada optimum memerlukan litar yang lebih dalam (lebih banyak lapisan QAOA), pemangkasan yang lebih lembut, atau perkakasan berhingar lebih rendah.\n"

